    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0455" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72113/704</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jefferson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-27T12:00:00-05:45">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1918, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received September 28, 5.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With respect to the loan of a special agent to the Nicaraguan Government as
                    outlined in the Department’s despatch No. 219, July 31, 1918.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d415-f1"/> President Chamorro informed me today that he would accept
                    the offer, and he is today telegraphing his Minister at Washington to this
                    effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
